Package: RAVEL
Title: Recovering Assortment-Adjusted Variance Explained by Genetic Liabilities
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Daniel", "Malawsky", , "d.malawsky@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4421-8688"))
Description: Structural equation modeling framework for estimating direct and
    indirect genetic effects on offspring phenotypes using parent-offspring trio
    data with polygenic scores. RAVEL accounts for measurement error in PGS,
    assortative mating, hidden genetic variants not captured by the PGS,
    cross-parent tagging confounds, and population stratification. The method
    uses latent variable modeling with multiple PGS indicators to correct for
    measurement error and provides unbiased estimates of direct child effects,
    maternal effects, paternal effects, and the degree of assortative mating.
